# Vouched contributors for JesusFilm/phoebe.
#
# Phoebe is an AFK coding agent pointed at this public repo, so anyone can open
# an issue or a PR here. This file is the explicit trust signal on the *author*
# of that work. See https://github.com/mitchellh/vouch for the system, and
# docs/trust.md for how it is wired up here and what a status actually means.
#
# Syntax:
#   - One handle per line (without @), sorted alphabetically.
#   - Optional platform prefix: platform:username (e.g., github:user).
#   - Denounce with minus prefix: -username or -platform:username.
#   - Optional details after a space following the handle.
#
# Collaborators with write access and bots are trusted automatically and do not
# need an entry. The maintainers below are listed anyway so this file states the
# trust set on its own, and so it survives a permission change. Bots are not
# listed: `gh-check-user` returns early on any handle ending in `[bot]`, before
# it ever reads this file, so an entry for one would be unreachable.
#
# `.github/workflows/vouch.yml` turns a status into an advisory `vouch:*` label.
# It never closes or locks anything — the gate on Phoebe picking work up is the
# `ready-for-agent` label, which only a maintainer can apply.
#
# Format, ordering, and duplicates are asserted by src/vouched-file.test.ts.
github:csiyang
github:mikeallisonJS
github:tataihono
